    "description": "Fatbeam is a fiber-network operator providing connectivity, transport, and related services to commercial, education, government, carrier, and residential customers. The business is infrastructure-led and asset-heavy because it owns and operates the underlying fiber network rather than acting solely as a reseller. Company materials describe a network footprint across eight western states and more than 150 cities, while sponsor materials previously referenced 1,250 route miles at the time of Basalt's acquisition. Its operating geography includes Washington, Oregon, Montana, Arizona, New Mexico, Idaho, Wyoming, and Nevada. The company was established in 2010 and has expanded its network reach through organic buildout and acquisitions. Basalt acquired Fatbeam from SDC Capital Partners and the company's founders in 2023, and public sources do not disclose the resulting ownership percentage.",
